    "id": "p22-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "40",
    "prompt": "Show that if $\\alpha+\\beta=\\frac\\pi3$, then $$(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha)(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\beta)=4.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha)(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\beta)=4$.\n\nTake tangent of the angle condition, use the sum formula, then rearrange and factorise.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\tan\\frac\\pi3=\\sqrt3\\\\\\frac{\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta&=\\sqrt3-\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta\\\\\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha+\\sqrt3\\tan\\beta+3\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta&=3\\\\1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha+\\sqrt3\\tan\\beta+3\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta&=4\\\\(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\alpha)(1+\\sqrt3\\tan\\beta)&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
